{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1082", "sample_idx": 31, "model_name": "google/gemma-3n-e2b-it", "content": "Arthur awoke to the insistent chirping of a digital bird. Sunlight streamed through a window that felt…wrong. Too perfect, too angled. He sat up, disoriented, and found himself in a room of vibrant, impossibly clean wood and polished stone. His clothes felt strangely…fitted. He glanced down and saw he was wearing a tunic and leather boots, not his usual worn jeans and t-shirt. A shimmering, almost imperceptible outline seemed to surround him, like a visual effect. He tried to reach for his glasses, but his hand passed right through the polished surface of a nearby table. Panic began to bubble in his chest. This wasn't his apartment. This wasn't real. He tried to speak, but the sound that came out was a perfectly rendered, slightly synthesized voice. \"Good morning, Adventurer!\" a cheerful, pixelated voice chirped from a nearby ornate mirror.\n\n***\n\nThe mirror, he quickly realized, was a character. And the \"Adventurer\" label wasn't a joke. He was standing in a meticulously crafted fantasy world, complete with bustling marketplaces, towering castles, and suspiciously cheerful NPCs. He felt the weight of a sword strapped to his back, a sword that felt strangely…familiar. He tried to remember how he got here, but his mind was a blank slate. The world seemed to react to his thoughts, the trees swaying with a gentle breeze he didn't feel, the cobblestones shifting slightly beneath his feet. A notification popped up in his vision: \"Quest: Retrieve the Sunstone from the Goblin King. Level 1.\" Arthur stared at the message, the digital bird chirping louder now, a mocking soundtrack to his utter bewilderment. He was trapped, it seemed, in a game he hadn't even known existed.\n\n\n\n", "logprobs": [{"token": "Arthur", "logprob": -0.7354406118392944}, {"token": "▁awoke", "logprob": -0.5281890630722046}, {"token": "▁to", "logprob": -0.003386716591194272}, {"tok